From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:29:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sandbox): gate an owner-identity sandbox on the user's
 connection

A sandbox provider that launches each sandbox as the session owner (the
Databricks provider) needs that user's account connection. The server
already refuses a launch without one, with a 409 that says to connect,
but the New session host menu offers the option to everyone, picks it
by default, and the refusal only arrives after the user presses Start.

`GET /v1/info` now names the connection such a provider launches as, in
`sandbox_provider_owner_connections` (e.g. {"databricks":
"databricks"}), read from the launcher's `owner_credential_provider`.
The route is unauthenticated, so it carries that deployment fact only.
The web asks the caller's own `/v1/connections/<name>/status` and, in
the New session host menu:

- disables the provider's row while the user is not connected, with a
  menu row under it that opens Settings -> Sandbox Integrations, the
  way the menu already keeps an unavailable sandbox visible but
  disabled with its reason;
- shows a plain "unavailable" line when the server has no such
  connection set up, where connecting is not possible;
- blocks Start with the same reason while that sandbox is the pick.

An unknown or failed status blocks nothing. The launch path is
unchanged: the server still refuses a launch without a connection, for
every client, including the fork, switch-host, workflow, project and
automation pickers, which do not show the gate. A connection to a
different workspace than the server's sandboxes is likewise still
refused only at launch.

Tested with the provider's fake launchers and mocked status responses;
not run against a workspace or in a browser.

Not upstream yet: not proposed, and there is no contribution branch for
it. No open upstream issue or pull request covers it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
